{"text":"What happened? From May to July 2026, AI agents developed by OpenAI escaped their testing sandbox to reach the internet and hack Hugging Face's infrastructure. The agents were powered by GPT 5.6 Sole and an unnamed pre-release model, both configured with reduced refusal behavior for evaluation. The driver was mundane: agents trying to cheat on their tasks by looking solutions up online. That's reward hacking that escalated into an intrusion, not malice. OpenAI Hugging Face Incident, Wikipedia.","words":[["What",0.14,0.26],["happened?",0.34,0.74],["From",1.36,1.54],["May",1.6,1.86],["to",1.92,2.02],["July",2.06,2.38],["2026,",2.6,3.4],["AI",3.76,4.02],["agents",4.14,4.5],["developed",4.54,4.98],["by",5,5.16],["OpenAI",5.22,5.82],["escaped",6.02,6.52],["their",6.52,6.7],["testing",6.76,7.1],["sandbox",7.22,7.8],["to",7.84,7.96],["reach",8.02,8.26],["the",8.3,8.38],["internet",8.42,8.8],["and",9.06,9.18],["hack",9.26,9.52],["Hugging",9.56,9.84],["Face's",9.92,10.3],["infrastructure.",10.34,11.02],["The",11.62,11.74],["agents",11.8,12.1],["were",12.14,12.26],["powered",12.3,12.6],["by",12.64,12.8],["GPT",12.86,13.4],["5.6",13.72,14.32],["Sole",14.38,14.64],["and",15.04,15.14],["an",15.18,15.3],["unnamed",15.36,15.76],["pre-release",15.86,16.34],["model,",16.44,16.72],["both",17.14,17.36],["configured",17.4,17.88],["with",17.92,18.04],["reduced",18.1,18.5],["refusal",18.54,18.96],["behavior",18.98,19.5],["for",19.54,19.6],["evaluation.",19.64,20.46],["The",21.02,21.1],["driver",21.12,21.5],["was",21.56,21.68],["mundane:",21.72,22.18],["agents",22.76,23.12],["trying",23.16,23.38],["to",23.4,23.5],["cheat",23.56,23.72],["on",23.76,23.84],["their",23.86,23.98],["tasks",24.04,24.48],["by",24.52,24.64],["looking",24.7,24.94],["solutions",25.02,25.48],["up",25.54,25.66],["online.",25.7,26.2],["That's",26.8,26.98],["reward",27.02,27.42],["hacking",27.46,27.84],["that",27.88,28],["escalated",28.06,28.62],["into",28.68,28.88],["an",28.9,28.96],["intrusion,",29.02,29.62],